I just wanted to thank the nethack development team for their 
efforts.  I've been running 3.1.1 on OS/2 2.x for a while, and it is 
outstanding & addictive.  Before that, I had run 3.0 under DOS a year 
or so ago.

This game gets better and better.  Of course, most of those who post 
here are either looking for spoilers or complaining about 
bugs/misfeatures.  The majority of happy hackers don't make 
themselves heard as often because they don't need to.  I'm sure the 
developers are aware of this "squeaky wheel gets the oil" rule, but 
just in case they forgot, thanks.

-Matt

p.s.--This is not intended as flame bait; I just wanted to take time 
out from bug reports and impatience over 3.1.2's availability to 
point out that we must all love this game, otherwise we wouldn't 
waste time in rec.games.hack.


